   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "A result is not yet a cause",
     "texto": [
      "**A practice report.** The data in this lesson are invented. When reading a **informe**, look at **what was measured**, **in whom** and **what the results allow us to say**.\n\n**Cautious words.** **Se observó**, **los datos sugieren**, **podría estar relacionado con**: they say there is a **relación**, but not that it is the **causa**. Data **sugieren**; they do not **demuestran**.\n\n**The limits.** Look for **limitaciones**: few plants, little time or no comparison group. With that you cannot **generalizar**.\n\n**Headline and report.** A headline can say more than the report. The authors **advierten** about their limits and ask for **prudencia**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "The language of caution",
     "texto": [
      "**Soft and strong verbs.** **Sugerir**, **indicar** and **parecer** leave the doubt open; **demostrar** and **probar** close it. A careful report uses the first.\n\n**Poder + estar relacionado con.** **Podría estar relacionado con** says it is possible, not certain.\n\n**Se + verb** gives the fact without saying who: **se observó**, **se registró**.\n\n**No se puede afirmar que + subjunctive**: **No se puede afirmar que el sol sea la causa.**\n\n**Mientras que** and **en cambio** set two facts against each other: **En ocho macetas se observó más crecimiento, mientras que en las otras cuatro no hubo cambios.**"
     ],
